{
  "question_id": "q_093_event_friends_rec",
  "slug": "event-friends-rec",
  "title": "Event Friends Recommendation",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "company": "Facebook",
  "premium": true,
  "question": "Facebook's social recommendations team wants to recommend upcoming events to users based on what their friends are attending.\n\n• `friendship_status` stores one row per direction with a `status` of `'friends'` or `'not_friends'`.\n• In `event_rsvp`, a person is **registered** for an event when their `attendance_status` is `'going'` (`'maybe'` and `'not_going'` do not count).\n\nRecommend an event to a user if **at least two of their friends** are registered for it and the user is not already registered for it themselves.\n\nWrite a query to output the `user_id` and the recommended `event_id`, sorted by `user_id` and then `event_id`.",
  "notes": [
    "Users 111, 222 and 333 are all friends of user 444.",
    "Friends 111 and 222 are going to event 789, so it is recommended to 444. Event 234 has three friends going, so it is recommended too."
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "friendship_status",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "user_a_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "user_b_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "status",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(50)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "table_name": "event_rsvp",
